    <h1>Telegram Bot Privacy Policy: What Telegram Requires and How to Write One</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Published October 2, 2026</p>

    <p>Telegram requires every bot and Mini App on the platform to have a privacy policy. The <a href="https://telegram.org/tos/bot-developers" rel="nofollow">Bot Developer Terms of Service</a> (Section 4) state that developers must maintain an accessible privacy policy detailing what data the bot stores, how it collects that data, and what it uses it for. Telegram provides a <a href="https://telegram.org/privacy-tpa" rel="nofollow">Standard Privacy Policy for Bots and Mini Apps</a> as a default, but any bot whose data practices go beyond what that template describes -- storing messages, calling third-party APIs, running payments, or collecting data the standard template does not account for -- must register a separate, custom privacy policy through <code>@BotFather</code>.</p>

    <p>This guide covers what Telegram actually checks, what data your bot receives through the Bot API that you need to disclose, the additional obligations Mini Apps and payment bots carry, how to handle GDPR and data retention, and a ready-to-copy sample policy you can adapt for your own bot. If you want a finished policy instead of writing one from scratch, <a href="https://buildprivacypolicy.com/">generate a privacy policy for free</a> and host it at a permanent URL.</p>

